[size=6][b]Ground Waypoints — planet markers on foot and on the hoverbike for SpaceBourne 2[/b][/size]

From your ship, SpaceBourne 2 marks a planet's outposts, cities, dungeons and mission sites. Land, step out or jump on the hoverbike, and those markers vanish: you cross the planet guessing. Ground Waypoints brings them back on the ground: a marker, the name and the distance, in the same colours the game uses from the ship.

Version 0.1.1 · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/13]Nexus Mods page[/url] · UE4SS Lua mod · works alone or with the rest of the realism set (see below). Idea by [b]TheCalcMan[/b] (Steam).

[line]
[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]On foot and on the hoverbike[/b], while you are on a planet's surface:
    - [b]places[/b]: outposts, cities, villages, camps, wrecks;
    - [b]locations[/b]: dungeons, caves and mission sites;
    - [b]points of interest[/b] nearby: crash sites, traders and the like.
[*][b]Same look as the ship's markers.[/b] Orange places, pink mission places, grey cleared dungeons. The name sits next to the marker with the distance below, in the game's format (152m, 3.4km).
[*][b]Arrows at the screen edge[/b] for the nearest places behind you or off screen, with their distance.
[*][b]Calm.[/b] At most 12 markers, nearest first (mission places always first). Nothing within 40 m (you are there). Points of interest only within 5 km; places and locations up to 600 km (a planet's outposts and dungeons are often 100–500 km apart).
[*][b]No double markers.[/b] Mission objectives and the few places the game already shows on the hoverbike stay the game's own.
[*][b]Out of the way.[/b] Hidden in the ship, in dungeons and stations, in photo mode, with a menu open, and when the game hides its HUD.
[*][b]On by default, no key needed.[/b] Markers appear on planets by themselves.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]SpaceBourne 2 (Steam).
[*][url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/releases/tag/v3.0.1]UE4SS 3.0.1[/url]. Installing HTR or the realism set installer installs it too.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Download GroundWaypoints-0.1.1.zip from the [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GroundWaypoints/releases]releases[/url].
[*]Extract it into the game folder (...\steamapps\common\SpaceBourne 2\). It adds SB2\Binaries\Win64\Mods\GroundWaypoints\; the enabled.txt inside turns it on.
[*]That's it: land on a planet and step out.
[/list]

Manual install: copy the GroundWaypoints folder from this repository into SpaceBourne 2\SB2\Binaries\Win64\Mods\.

Uninstall: delete SB2\Binaries\Win64\Mods\GroundWaypoints. Ground Waypoints never writes to your saves.

[line]
[size=5][b]Controls[/b][/size]

No key needed: markers show on planets automatically. To add an on/off key, set ToggleKey in scripts\config.lua (for example "0").

[line]
[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]

Edit Mods\GroundWaypoints\scripts\config.lua. Every line is optional.

[list]
[*]Enabled: false switches the mod off completely.
[*]StartOn: start with the markers shown (true) or hidden.
[*]ToggleKey: none by default; for example "0" to add an on/off key.
[*]OnFoot / OnHoverbike: where markers show.
[*]Places / Locations / PointsOfInterest: what is marked.
[*]MaxDistance (600 000 m), PoiMaxDistance (5 000 m), HideWithinMeters (40 m).
[*]MaxMarkers (12), OffscreenArrows and MaxOffscreenArrows (4).
[*]Look: MarkerSize, TextScale, HeightOffset, ShowNames, and Colors.
[/list]

The text follows the game's own [b]indicator scale[/b] setting, like the ship's markers.

[line]
[size=5][b]How it works[/b][/size]

The game draws all its markers on the HUD canvas (Q1Hud). On foot its planet-place function stops at once, and on the hoverbike it only draws an active mission's site. There is no switch to flip, so Ground Waypoints draws the markers itself on the same canvas, with the game's own font, icons and colours. It reads the places' positions and names a few times a second and keeps only plain data; each frame it only places and draws the markers. Details: DESIGN.md.

[line]
[size=5][b]Status and known limits[/b][/size]

Tested in game on 2026-10-31 on planet Oclite (details in DESIGN.md, section 8):
[list]
[*]on foot and on the hoverbike, the markers, names, distances and edge arrows;
[*]the optional 0 key (the game does nothing else with it);
[*]the game's own markers (your ship) unchanged;
[*]12 markers at once, up to 460 km away;
[*]frame times with the mod on vs off: no measurable difference (120 vs 118 fps, same median and p99);
[*]your saves untouched.
[/list]

Known limits:

[list]
[*][b]Only what the planet has loaded.[/b] Places appear once the game has created them, as in the ship.
[*][b]Point-of-interest names come from the game's internal names[/b] ("Ship Crash", "Raided House"…), so they are in English.
[*][b]Two places in the same direction[/b] can overlap their labels.
[*][b]If the mod is reloaded mid-game[/b], the first time you step out on a planet it may search once for places it missed: about 0.2 s of small stutters.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Part of the SpaceBourne 2 realism set[/b][/size]

Part of the realism set, built around [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/4]Hardcore Tactical Realism[/url] as the core mod. HTR is not required: this mod works on its own or with any of the others. To install them all at once, use the installer: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-Realism]SpaceBourne 2 Realism[/url] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/11]Nexus[/url]).

[list]
[*][b]Hardcore Tactical Realism (HTR) — realistic ballistics and tactical AI[/b]: released: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HardcoreTacticalRealism]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/4]Nexus Mods[/url] · [url=https://steamcommunity.com/app/1646850/discussions/0/573805072991123580]Steam discussion[/url]
[*][b]Split Controls — separate invert for ship and on foot[/b]: released: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SplitControls]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/5]Nexus Mods[/url]
[*][b]Silent Ops — realistic stealth[/b]: released: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SilentOps]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/6]Nexus Mods[/url]
[*][b]Gear Without Levels — use gear regardless of level[/b]: released: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GearWithoutLevels]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/7]Nexus Mods[/url]
[*][b]SB2 HOTAS — HOTAS, triple screens, head tracking[/b]: released: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HOTAS]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/8]Nexus Mods[/url]
[*][b]Faction Power — your deeds earn your faction power[/b]: released: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-FactionPower]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/9]Nexus Mods[/url]
[*][b]Tactical Engineering — realistic deployable turrets[/b]: released: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-TacticalEngineering]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/10]Nexus Mods[/url]
